Additional obligations (Citadel project)
----------------------------------------

1. Preserve product names — Do not rename or remove Citadel, Fortress,
   or Keep where they appear in this repository (source identifiers, UI copy,
   docs, bundle IDs, module names, or user-facing labels). You may change behavior
   and add features; you may not strip or replace these names.

2. Preserve the logo and official branding — Do not replace or remove the
   Citadel logo and official branding assets shipped in this repository, including
   Resources/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/,
   Resources/Assets.xcassets/CitadelMark.imageset/,
   Resources/Assets.xcassets/AisanceMark.imageset/, and related artwork under
   docs/assets/. You may add assets; you may not swap official marks for a
   different product identity.

3. Keep upstream branding and naming updates — When you merge from or track
   this project, preserve future updates to product names, logos, and branding
   assets from upstream. Do not permanently fork off and block or discard later
   official naming or branding changes from this repository.

4. Keep project notices — Preserve this file, NOTICES.md, ATTRIBUTIONS.md,
   and CHANGELOG.md (or their substance) in source and binary distributions.


Apache License 2.0 obligations (summary)
----------------------------------------

In addition to the items above, Apache-2.0 requires you to:

1. Keep copyright and license notices — Include the Apache-2.0 copyright and
   license statements in redistributions.
2. State changes — If you distribute modified files, include a prominent notice
   that you changed them.
3. Include NOTICE text — Pass through any NOTICE entries from files that contain
   them (see Apache-2.0 section 4(d)).
4. Third-party components — Honor upstream licenses for bundled or referenced
   software (e.g. CoworkCore / AionCore). See ATTRIBUTIONS.md.
5. No implied endorsement — Do not use contributor names or trademarks to
   endorse a derivative product without permission.

Patent rights and termination rules are defined in the full License (sections 3, 5–6).


